# PM-v2 generated data and research provenance stay local or in the
# content-addressed artifact vault.  Public, sanitized summaries should be
# promoted into docs/ explicitly instead of committing an entire run folder.
/project/data/pm_v2/
/project/data/pm_v1_5/
/project/outputs/pm_v2*/
/project/outputs/pm_v1_5*/
/project/outputs/strategy_rag_v1_*/
/project/outputs/evoemo_fixed_tracks_v22/
/project/outputs/evoemo_fixed_tracks_v1_5/
/project/outputs/evoemo_pm_v2*/
/project/outputs/evoemo_pm_v1_5*/
/project/outputs/evoemo_pmv22*/
/project/outputs/posthoc_v1_bank_mechanism_diagnostic*/
/project/outputs/posthoc_v1_bank*/
/project/outputs/v1_bank_causal_probe*/
/project/outputs/v1_5_*/

# 2026-08-05 git-recovery audit: the prefix-specific rules above have fallen
# behind the current output-naming conventions (e.g. esconv_auxiliary_*,
# evoemo_fixed_tracks_v1_5_v2/v3_*, evoemo_selective*, full_judging_*,
# synthetic_sweep, and hundreds of loose top-level files directly under
# outputs/) -- none of those matched the old patterns and were sitting
# untracked-but-stageable. Every entry under outputs/ that this repo has
# produced is a pipeline run artifact (readiness reports, generation/judging
# candidates, human-review packets, private per-run jsonl); see
# project/docs/GIT_RECOVERY_INVENTORY_20260805.json for the full catalogued
# list (category, size, file count) taken before this rule was added.
# Ignore the whole directory; promote sanitized conclusions into docs/
# explicitly per run, as the comment above already said to do.
/project/outputs/

# Same problem on the data/ side: these are pipeline-generated candidate/
# repro/confirmation snapshots, not curated inputs. data/pm_v1_5_contracts/,
# data/strategy/, and data/external/ are curated/contract content and must
# stay tracked -- do not broaden these patterns to catch them.
/project/data/esconv_auxiliary_v1_5*/
/project/data/esconv_test_v1_5*/
/project/data/pm_v1_5_evo_style_synthetic_memory_v1_candidate/
/project/data/pm_v1_5_final_*/
/project/data/pm_v1_5_formal_v8_*/
/project/data/pm_v1_5_v3_*/
/project/data/pm_v1_5_v5_2_confirmation_v1/

# Provider payloads, generated call plans, local checkpoints, and completed
# reviews belong in the private vault regardless of their parent directory.
**/raw_api_calls.jsonl
**/raw_seeker_calls.jsonl
**/raw_*_calls.jsonl
**/*call_plan*.jsonl
**/paired_generations.jsonl
**/pilot_bundle.json
**/*.joblib
**/reviewer_*_completed.csv
**/annotations_completed*.csv

# Local migration/integrity reports contain machine paths and immediately
# become stale when the workspace changes.
/MIGRATION_REPORT_ZH.md
/MIGRATION_SHA256SUMS.txt
/project/migration_preflight.json

# Never stage private blinding maps or append-only paid-attempt provenance by
# accident, even when they are created outside the standard PM-v2 directories.
**/private_condition_mapping.jsonl
**/physical_attempt_ledger.jsonl
**/failed_attempt_*.json
